> **Context**: These prompts are designed for **Google Stitch 2.0** to generate high-fidelity UI mockups
> for the {{Product Name}} {{Scope}}. Each prompt block represents **one user flow** (multiple screens).

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Stitch 2.0 Workflow**
>
> 1. **Load** `DESIGN.md` into Stitch project workspace (one-time setup per project)
> 2. **Select** the Design System via the Design System Picker in Stitch UI
> 3. **Generate** flows using the prompts below (each prompt → multi-screen flow)
> 4. **Edit** individual screens/elements using conversational refinement
> 5. **Prototype** — connect screens into interactive clickable flows
>
> Design tokens are **NOT** inlined in each prompt — Stitch 2.0 reads them from `DESIGN.md` automatically.

> **Prompt Conventions**
> - Each prompt uses the **PTCF framework** (Persona → Task → Context → Format)
> - `F.x`: User Flow prompts (multi-screen journeys)
> - `E.x`: Edit/Refinement prompts (post-generation adjustments)
> - `R.x`: Redesign prompts (style iteration on existing screens)

