## Quality Checklist

### Design System Compliance
- [ ] `DESIGN.md` is loaded in Stitch project workspace
- [ ] Design System Picker is set to the correct system
- [ ] All screens use token-driven styles (no hard-coded values)
- [ ] Colors match semantic roles defined in DESIGN.md

### Flow Coverage
- [ ] All user journeys from PRD are covered (cross-reference with PRD)
- [ ] Each flow covers: default / loading / empty / error states
- [ ] Navigation is consistent across all flows
- [ ] Responsive layouts verified (desktop + mobile at minimum)

### Component Consistency
- [ ] Buttons: same sizes and styles for same-level actions across flows
- [ ] Typography: consistent heading hierarchy
- [ ] Cards/Tables: uniform padding, radius, shadow
- [ ] Feedback: consistent toast/alert/empty-state patterns

### Prototype & Handoff
- [ ] Key flows connected as interactive prototypes
- [ ] Transitions are smooth and logical
- [ ] No dead-end screens (all have navigation back)
- [ ] Code export validated (if applicable)

### Content Quality
- [ ] No leaked internal technical terms in user-facing copy
- [ ] Real-looking (not Lorem ipsum) placeholder content
- [ ] All labels and CTAs are actionable and clear

